  "rai:dataCollection": "This release is derived from existing public composed image retrieval benchmarks. It was created by first running a cross-retriever shortcut audit over the official benchmark queries, then collecting structured human validity judgments over the shortcut-free residue.",
  "rai:dataCollectionType": [
    "Secondary Data Analysis",
    "Manual Human Curator",
    "Software Collection"
  ],
  "rai:dataCollectionRawData": "The source data are the official benchmark query files and image identifiers for the fashioniq benchmark together with the corresponding retrieval outputs stored in this release.",
  "rai:dataPreprocessingProtocol": [
    "Aggregate per-retriever multimodal, text-only, and image-only ranks into a dataset-level shortcut audit using retrieval cutoff K=10.",
    "Use random seed 123 for stochastic sampling and release construction steps.",
    "Export the shortcut-free union as tabular trace records with relative image references only.",
    "Filter the human-validation release to retained queries and flatten nested fields for Croissant-friendly CSV export."
  ],
  "rai:dataAnnotationProtocol": "Shortcut-free queries were inspected by trained annotators using a shared protocol. Annotators judged whether the reference image, textual edit, and target image form a coherent composed image retrieval instance, and if invalid they marked one or more of four reasons: invalid text query, invalid image query, invalid target image, or overly broad query.",
